    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 28,
    "summary": "Tyre and Sidon will fall and be destroyed—The Lord will gather the people of Israel to their own land—They will then dwell safely.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The word of the Lord came again unto me, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 28:1",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Son of man, say unto the prince of Tyrus, Thus saith the Lord God; Because thine heart is lifted up, and thou hast said, I am a God, I sit in the seat of God, in the midst of the seas; yet thou art a man, and not God, though thou set thine heart as the heart of God:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          },
          {
            "start": 200,
            "end": 203,
            "text": "Isa. 55:8 (8–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 87,
