        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, thou art wiser than Daniel; there is no secret that they can hide from thee:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Ezek. 14:14; Dan. 9:22 (22–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 28:3",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "With thy wisdom and with thine understanding thou hast gotten thee riches, and hast gotten gold and silver into thy treasures:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 28:4",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "By thy great wisdom and by thy traffick hast thou increased thy riches, and thine heart is lifted up because of thy riches:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:28 (28–29), 42; Hel. 1:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 28:5",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord God; Because thou hast set thine heart as the heart of God;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 28:6",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, therefore I will bring strangers upon thee, the terrible of the nations: and they shall draw their swords against the beauty of thy wisdom, and they shall defile thy brightness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 113,
            "text": "Ezek. 30:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
